# Direct dependencies of the backend image (see Dockerfile) and of the
# local development environment. Hash-Lock folgt spaeter -- requirements.txt
# is currently a plain `pip freeze` of the resolved tree, not a
# `pip-compile --generate-hashes` lock (see requirements.txt's own header),
# same as Weave-Retrieval's/Weave-Knowledge's backend/requirements.in.
#
# fastapi/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pytest/httpx/PyYAML pins are kept
# identical to Weave-Retrieval's backend/requirements.in -- no reason for
# these to drift between sibling services without cause. Deliberately NO
# sqlalchemy/alembic/celery/redis here: Weave-Runtime is the stateless
# bot-orchestrator (see README's "Nicht-Ziele") -- it owns no schema to
# migrate and no task queue to run, only synchronous HTTP calls out to
# Weave-Retrieval or an LLM provider (httpx) and YAML bot configs (PyYAML, see
# app/services/botconfig.py).
#
# langgraph/langchain-core (rollout plan "Schritt 3 -- LangGraph mit mehreren
# Subagenten", app/services/agent_graph.py): the one deliberate exception to
# the "no framework, just httpx" posture above. The multi-subagent
# orchestrator-worker flow -- parallel fan-out capped by `max_concurrency`,
# map-reduce result merging, budget-aware follow-up rounds -- is exactly
# the state-machine-with-parallel-branches problem LangGraph's `StateGraph`/
# `Send` already solve correctly (cancellation-safe fan-out, a documented
# concurrent-update contract for merged state); hand-rolling that
# scheduling/merging logic with bare `threading`/`queue` (as this module's
# own n8n-streaming code already does for a much simpler single-worker case)
# would reproduce a materially more complex, materially less tested version
# of the same thing. `langchain-core` is pulled in transitively for
# `RunnableConfig` (the one type this module needs to pass `max_concurrency`
# through to `graph.invoke()`) and is pinned directly here rather than left
# implicit, so a future `langgraph` upgrade can't silently drift it.
langgraph==1.2.11
langchain-core==1.6.3
fastapi==0.141.1
uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4
pydantic==2.13.5
pydantic-settings==2.15.0
httpx==0.28.1
PyYAML==6.0.3
